  "id": "common-metric",
  "term": "common metric",
  "definition": "In this context, a common metric is the usual standard used to judge performance on a test. For phonemic verbal fluency, the common metric has been the total number of words produced, even though the source notes that this single measure may not capture the full complexity of performance.",
